.TH HYPR-DE 7 "2026-08-15" "hypr-DE" "hypr-DE"
.SH NAME
hypr-de \- packaged Hyprland desktop configuration
.SH DESCRIPTION
hypr-DE is a packaged Hyprland configuration and the runtime packages that
session needs. It is not a greeter session and does not register a desktop
environment. Log into
.B Hyprland (uwsm-managed)
from the Hyprland package.
.PP
Configs and styles are package-owned under
.I /usr
and
.IR /etc/xdg .
Home carries only what you own:
.IR ~/.config/hypr/local.lua ,
monitor profiles, wallpaper, and optional module or unit overrides.
.SH SESSION
.TP
.B Login
Pick Hyprland (uwsm-managed) at the greeter. hypr-DE supplies
.I /etc/xdg/uwsm
env files and user units; it does not add a competing session entry.
.TP
.B Config load order
.I /etc/xdg/hypr/hyprland.lua
dofiles the packaged
.I @DATADIR@/hypr/main.lua ,
then pcall's
.I ~/.config/hypr/local.lua
(last-wins). Monitor layouts belong in
.I ~/.config/hypr/profiles/
(hyprstate selects the matching profile). Putting monitors in local.lua
clobbers that.
.TP
.B Theme
.B SUPER+T
runs
.B lmtt switch
(see
.BR lmtt (1)).
GTK follows the XDG appearance portal. Qt apps that use qt6ct get an
LMTT-owned color scheme at
.I ~/.config/qt6ct/colors/lmtt.conf
and a merged
.B [Appearance]
section; Fonts and other qt6ct keys stay yours.
.TP
.B Bar
Waybar is the shell. Workspace buttons come from waybar-workspace-buttons.
.TP
.B Lock
.B SUPER+L
is
.B loginctl lock-session .
hypridle's lock_cmd answers that signal, so the key, idle timeout, and
suspend share one lock screen (vigil-lock).
.TP
.B Files
.B SUPER+E
opens Nautilus.
.TP
.B Bluetooth
Waybar's bluetooth module is the indicator (no tray applet). Left-click
opens Overskride; right-click toggles adapter power.
.TP
.B Audio
Volume keys use
.B wpctl .
pavucontrol is the app mixer; hyprpwcenter (SHIFT+XF86AudioPlay) is the
patchbay.
.SH SCRATCHPAD AND ZONES
.B SUPER+S
and
.B SUPER+0
toggle the named scratchpad
.I special:magic .
That is built-in Hyprland and needs no plugin.
.PP
Each numeric workspace can also own
.I special:N
via the workspace-zones plugin. See
.BR workspace-zones (7).
.B SUPER+ALT+S
toggles the focused workspace's zone;
.B SUPER+ALT+SHIFT+S
moves the focused window into it;
.B SUPER+CTRL+ALT+S
stashes without following. If the plugin is not loaded, those binds log a
Lua error instead of silently doing nothing.
.SH KEYBINDS
.B SUPER+/
opens
.BR hypr-de-help (1),
which lists every bind from the running compositor (including local.lua)
and explains the session.
.B SUPER+SHIFT+/
opens the same list as a fuzzel dmenu for quick search.
.PP
Every packaged bind carries
.B desc = "Category: text"
so the help window and cheatsheet can group and filter. Follow that
convention in local.lua; undescribed binds show as (custom).
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /etc/xdg/hypr/hyprland.lua
XDG entry that loads the packaged config.
.TP
.I @DATADIR@/hypr/main.lua
Packaged binds, rules, and autostart.
.TP
.I @DATADIR@/hypr/local.lua.example
Template for
.IR ~/.config/hypr/local.lua .
.TP
.I ~/.config/hypr/local.lua
User overrides (last-wins).
.TP
.I ~/.config/hypr/profiles/
hyprstate monitor profiles.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR hypr-de-help (1),
.BR workspace-zones (7),
.BR lmtt (1)
